# CODEOWNERS — Discovery Catalog
#
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners. Order matters:
# later patterns take precedence over earlier ones. Maintainers listed for a
# path are auto-requested for review on any PR that touches the path.
#
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-customization/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Only security-sensitive or executable content has explicit owners. Ordinary
# Markdown and data manifests use the repository's general review policy
# without notifying every maintainer.

# CI / workflow tooling
/.github/workflows/                     @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer
/.github/scripts/                       @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer

# Validation policy — the approved base images, source allowlist, tag taxonomy,
# rule waivers, and ratchet baseline. Editing these changes what the catalog
# will accept, so the gate must be explicit rather than inherited from `*`.
/.github/policy/                        @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer
/.github/policy/baseline.json           @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer
/docs/validation-baseline-debt.md       @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer

# Schema files — changes here can break every agent/kit in the catalog.
/docs/schemas/                          @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer

# Auto-generated registries — should normally never be hand-edited (see
# POL-011). Bot-authored refresh PRs still require a human CODEOWNER approval.
/.auto-registry/                        @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer

# Per-content area
/agents/                                @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer
/starter-kits/                          @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer

# Executable operator utilities. Discovery Toolbox release PRs intentionally
# use the repository's ordinary one-approval rule (empty-owner) instead of requiring a
# specific CODEOWNER; REL-002 verifies the VSIX pointer and digest.
/utilities/                            @microsoft/discovery-samples-maintainer
/utilities/discovery-toolbox
